<newsitem itemid="399723" id="root" date="1997-02-24" xml:lang="en">
<title>PORTUGAL: LBSH issues 5 bln esc Navigator bond.</title>
<headline>LBSH issues 5 bln esc Navigator bond.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced by lead manager banks Banco Portugues de Investimento (BPI) and Argentaria.</p>
<p>BORROWER: Landesbank Schleswig Holstein Girozentrale LSHG.D (LBSH)</p>
<p>RATING: IBCA AAA and Moody's Aa1, independently of statute of debt</p>
<p>STATUTE: Subordinated debt</p>
<p>AMT: 5 billion escudos</p>
<p>FIXED INTEREST RATE: 6.76 percent</p>
<p>MATURITY: 10 years</p>
<p>TYPE: Navigator</p>
<p>SUBSCRIPTION PRICE: 100 percent</p>
<p>NOMINAL VALUE: 100 escudos per share</p>
<p>SUBSCRIPTION DATE: 26 March 1997</p>
<p>REIMBURSEMENT DATE: 26 March 2007</p>
<p>LAW APPLIED: English, subordination clauses subject to German law</p>
<p>QUOTED: Luxembourg bourse</p>
<p>NATIONAL PAYING AGENT: Banco Portugues de Investimento (BPI) -- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
